{"archetypes":[{"name":"pricing-pipeline","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The migration depends on token-cost.sh remaining authoritative while Python handles mixed bucket/blended vendor pricing and fallback paths.","prompt_body":"Investigate the report_tokens_cost and report_tokens_render paths for any divergence from the plan's pricing authority contract. Check whether per-vendor bucket handling, KV parsing, env rate forwarding, fallback warnings, and rendered headline totals preserve the intended semantics. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"issue-posting","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"GitHub issue creation now combines repo slug resolution, redaction, byte trimming, and gh wrapper behavior where silent failures were explicitly in scope.","prompt_body":"Review the report_tokens_issue, gh.issue_create, scan repo resolution, and CLI orchestration flow for failure propagation and body-size handling. Pay special attention to redaction order, UTF-8 byte measurement, immutable truncation banners, repo omission behavior, and non-zero exits for gh failures. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"quiet-wrapper","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The bash wrapper must restore stdout and stderr under lib-quiet before execing Python so operator-visible contracts remain intact.","prompt_body":"Inspect the rewritten run-analysis.sh and quiet-mode harness for file descriptor restoration, argument validation, env flag pass-through, and diagnostics visibility. Verify that quiet mode cannot swallow stdout, stderr warnings, cache output, or removed-flag errors. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"scan-semantics","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The scanner is responsible for preserving fail-soft log ingestion while changing from legacy report parsing to committed larch-log records.","prompt_body":"Examine report_tokens_scan and its tests for faithful handling of malformed manifests, timing files, run params, token reports, missing pricing fields, limits, workflow classification, and design versus implement basenames. Check that skip-versus-default decisions match the plan and do not silently create zero-cost or misclassified runs. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"plot-isolation","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Matplotlib must stay outside the stdlib-only python tree while still honoring the committed plot schema and persistent output lifetime.","prompt_body":"Review report_tokens_plot, plot-cost-over-time.py, the schema docs, and tests for the subprocess isolation boundary. Check that sys.executable, runner injection, MPLCONFIGDIR, child JSON contracts, no-plot handling, matplotlib-missing behavior, and persistent PNG paths align with the plan. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-parity","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds pytest to harness shards and touches Python parity tests, Makefile shard registration, and relevant-check selection.","prompt_body":"Inspect CI workflow dependency changes, Makefile phony/shard registration, pytest harness targets, and relevant-checks updates for drift or missing coverage. Verify that new tests are reachable in both local and CI paths without accidentally pulling heavy lint dependencies into the harness job. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
